    "summary": "I built the three bases joined at one corner, with a stud spike facing down under that corner. The configurator found no rule issues and no mesh collisions.\n\nThe original base stays at (0,0), and I added two full bases at (1,0) and (0,1). Each one touches the other two, so all three meet at a single corner. The configurator offered exactly one downward stud spike site, at that shared corner, and I placed the spike there.\n\nFollowing the house rules, I also capped the 12 open outer faces with solid end caps and bolted the 3 shared walls with joint bolts so the bases can't slide apart. That brings the build to 16 parts, about 1,095 g of filament.",
